# Unit 2

## Run Log — Before

| Criterion | Target | Run 1 | Run 2 | Run 3 | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Retrieved chunk contains the answer | 4 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 2. Every answer names a source | 5 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 3. Gate stops out-of-corpus questions | 4 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 4. Sampled chunks read as complete thoughts | 4 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |
| 5. Responses include exact target values/phrases | 5 of 5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 | MET |

## Verdicts

| # | Criterion | Verdict | How I decided |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Retrieved chunk contains the answer | MET | All 5 test questions successfully retrieved the correct document chunks across all 3 runs, confirmed by inspection of generation outputs and source lists. |
| 2 | Every answer names a source | MET | Every single generated response across all 3 evaluation runs successfully cited its source file inline. |
| 3 | Gate stops out-of-corpus questions | MET | The relevance gate successfully refused all 5 out-of-scope test questions (yielding distance scores between `0.824` and `0.923`, well above the `0.6` cutoff). |
| 4 | Sampled chunks read as complete thoughts | MET | Inspection of chunk boundaries confirmed that paragraph-based splitting successfully kept thoughts intact without splitting sentences in half. |
| 5 | Responses include exact target values/phrases | MET | The prompt configuration successfully forced Gemini to output precise target details and metrics matching expectations. |

## Diagnoses

**Misses:** None. All five evaluation criteria achieved a 100% pass rate across all three test runs. 

**Analysis:** Because no criteria were missed, the system did not encounter pipeline failures at the loading, chunking, embedding, retrieval, or generation stages during baseline evaluation. However, clearing all criteria on the first try indicates that our targets were set conservatively safe rather than probing the limits of the system. 

If we were to tighten the evaluation for a subsequent iteration, we would increase the target string-matching constraints for Criterion 5 or lower the relevance gate cutoff to test boundary discrimination on ambiguous queries.

